 "notes": [
  "SRD 5.2.1 prints one subclass per class; each class's subclasses list is exactly what the SRD has.",
  "features_by_level maps a class level (a string) to the subclass features gained there, in SRD order; only levels with features appear.",
  "feature_levels maps each subclass feature to the class level that grants it, for reading a subclass off an existing sheet.",
  "subclass_level is the class level of the '<Class> Subclass' choice; subclass_feature_levels are the levels where the class table says 'Subclass feature'. The subclass's feature levels are exactly subclass_level plus those.",
  "feature_index maps every subclass feature name to the class, subclass and level that grant it.",
  "Text is ASCII: curly apostrophes became straight ones."
 ],
